xt{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535484 17592186045443 false] [17592186342180 1071 "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139535484 17592186045443 true] [17592186342180 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$" 13194139535484 17592186045443 false] [17592186342180 1074 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\b